WEBVTT

00:00.360 --> 00:03.160
You have to make an important decision.

00:03.160 --> 00:09.760
Four pieces of new information arrive, one at a time, then nothing more comes.

00:16.600 --> 00:21.500
This is all the information you're going to get, and the decision is due now.

00:21.500 --> 00:23.900
What do you notice right away?

00:23.900 --> 00:28.000
The pull to wait, the urge to move, something else?

00:44.700 --> 00:49.800
How much certainty do you need before you're willing to move?

00:49.800 --> 00:52.600
Most people never test that level.

00:52.600 --> 00:56.400
You're about to find out what yours is.

00:56.400 --> 00:58.500
Here are your options.

00:58.500 --> 01:01.100
Act with what you know.

01:01.100 --> 01:06.100
Ask for one more missing input that matters most.

01:06.100 --> 01:08.900
Push the decision to someone else.

01:08.900 --> 01:10.900
Wait for more certainty.

01:26.300 --> 01:33.500
Now, new decision, same amount of information as before, four pieces of six.

01:33.500 --> 01:35.500
What do you do this time?

01:46.600 --> 01:52.400
You just tested your comfort zone and change in one sitting.

01:52.400 --> 01:58.200
This week, notice one real decision where you're waiting for more certainty than you actually need,

01:58.200 --> 02:03.600
and practice taking action with incomplete information.
